    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>This ornate helm is steeped in the power of domination, a form of runic magic meant to crush the will of another being utterly. Together with its companion Artifact, @UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.items.Item.oBl3Opv2ShJ55zDF]{Frostmourne}, the helm allowed its wearers—three successive Lich Kings—to rule the Scourge.</p><p><strong>Attuning to the Helm.</strong> When you attune to the helm, make a DC 18 Charisma saving throw. On a successful save, you take 10d6 Psychic damage. On a failed save, your soul merges with the Lich King, who takes control of your body like a puppet, and you become an NPC under the DM’s control.</p><p>While attuned to the helm, you are unwilling to part with it, wearing it at all times, and you can’t voluntarily end your Attunement to it.</p><p><strong>Properties of the Helm.</strong> While attuned to the helm, your alignment is Neutral Evil, and you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Command the Scourge.</strong> As a Magic action, you can send a psychic command to every Undead that belongs to the Scourge. Make an ability check using your spellcasting ability (DC 20). On a success, you can give the Undead Scourge a general command, such as “attack any creature you come across” or “guard my stronghold,” or give a specific member of the Scourge a command, such as “deliver a plague to Stormwind.” Whether or not you succeed, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Truesight.</strong> You have Truesight with a range of 120 feet.</p></li><li><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> The helm has 8 charges and regains 1d4 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it (save DC 18), expending the number of charges it shows.</p></li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplAnimateDea]{Animate Dead}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplClairvoyan]{Clairvoyance}</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDream00000]{Dream}</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSpeakwithD]{Speak with Dead}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.spells.Item.LRTqRB6zRyXxIhnb]{Telepathy}</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWordofReca]{Word of Recall}</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The <em>Helm of Domination</em> has the following random properties:</p><ul><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 minor detrimental property</p></li><li><p>1 major detrimental property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Destroying the Helm of Domination.</strong> The helm shatters if it is struck by a blade forged in the Shadowlands. Only the Runecarver, who forged it in the first place, can reforge it from the fragments.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-txoYSAdrxW0ADhFx\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ. <em>Attunement Ordeal</em> fait le jet : ses 10d6 Psychic s’appliquent sur une réussite ; sur un échec, la créature devient un PNJ du MJ, à appliquer à la main. <em>Command the Scourge</em> compte l’utilisation du jour : faites le test (DD 20) avec votre caractéristique d’incantation. <em>Telepathy</em> vient du compendium Spells.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
